                "retweet_count": 1,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "I met with AFT CT nurses from Backus Hospital in Norwich and Lawrence + Memorial Hospital in New London to discuss the impending impacts of Medicaid cuts in the \u201cBig Beautiful Bill\u201d. \n\nThese cuts will leave 10 million people newly uninsured, putting huge stress on emergency rooms and forcing hospitals to scale back services for everyone. It\u2019s not too late to stop this. Congress must reverse these health care cuts. \n\nThank you to Heather Brauth, President of the Backus Federation of Nurses AFT CT Local 5149, and John Brady, Vice President of AFT CT, for hosting me.",
                "text_lang": "en",
